1514	As demonstrated in the previous section, the high-multiplicity final states allow us to further suppress the backgrounds by demanding cuts of $N^{\rm iso}_{\rm jets}\geq 2$ and  $M_J > 650 \GeV$. Finally, we apply at least $1b$-tag on both of the boosted top jets, and at least $1b$-tag on the isolated jets (abbreviated to $3b$-tag). Since we lost a substantial amount of signal events at the ditop selection already, we are not able to do a $4b$-tag in this case.
