1582	In the boosted regime, on the other hand, two boosted tops from a heavy resonance decay are characteristically differentiated from two non-boosted spectator tops in terms of $p_T$ scales, resolving the combinatoric issue. Also we can exploit the fact that their decay products are strongly collimated rendering an easy and simple way to reconstruct them. In this section, we demonstrate the capability of reconstructing a resonance using jet-substructure methods as well as a collinear approximation, and then reassess the sensitivity of the SSDL channel.
